{"author":{"id":"a0bedcda7d4818e8dd17decd7a985870a73dfe301f9778312ef9f6a894918ace"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1774583016,"nonce":"eUTE3hFbqxWvngphPLxmeu9Dt3Y=","metadata":{"github-id":"I_kwDOCGKeh873TMzm","github-url":"https://github.com/git-bug/git-bug/issues/1543","origin":"github"},"title":"Control UI / webchat does not render TTS audio replies, even though MP3 files are generated server-side","message":"Summary\nWith messages.tts.auto = \"always\" enabled, the local Control UI / webchat shows plain text only. No audio player or file attachment appears. If inline [[tts:...]] directives are used, they are displayed literally instead of being interpreted.\n\nEnvironment\n\nOpenClaw: 2026.3.24\nSurface: Control UI / local webchat\nBrowser: Google Chrome\nOS: Linux\nGateway: localhost / loopback\nConfig\n\nSteps to reproduce\n\nEnable TTS with messages.tts.auto = \"always\"\nOpen local Control UI in Chrome\nSend: reply with one short sentence only\nObserve response\nOptional: test an inline directive like [[tts:voice=en-US-MichelleNeural]] hello\nExpected\n\nWebchat shows playable audio attachment or inline audio control\nInline TTS directives are interpreted, not shown raw\nActual\n\nReply is plain text only\nNo audio/file attachment is shown\n[[tts:...]] is displayed literally\nAdditional evidence\nTTS synthesis is succeeding server-side. Generated files exist, e.g.:\n\n/tmp/openclaw/tts-NxKKM3/voice-1774582095377.mp3\n/tmp/openclaw/tts-duJjSU/voice-1774582017272.mp3\nSo this appears to be a Control UI / webchat delivery or rendering issue, not just provider config.","files":null}]}